  '1901',
  'The Union Pacific Railroad\'s Bridge and Building Department put up this depot in 1901 on the main line, which had reached Manhattan in 1866. Theodore Roosevelt spoke to students from the back of his train here, and Woodrow Wilson and Franklin Roosevelt also stopped at it. Its present look comes from a restoration finished in 2006.',
